{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"8163df785747a46b75a398666f3bdf9b5abed42d0376cfce50f265f09b8c5198","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_5f3b3d7cc9685c3fee283533d0e6b92635ac12876ecad41724c5b388a35cd586","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a coherent and technically sound architecture for tree-structured decoding. The methodological formulation is clear, and the experimental design is appropriate for the scope of the work, effectively validating the core claims on both synthetic and real-world data. However, the submission lacks sufficient detail on hyperparameters and code availability, which limits reproducibility. Additionally, the statistical rigor is limited by the absence of variance reporting or significance tests for the reported improvements.","paper_id":"HkYhZDqxg","paper_identity_sha256":"07a443f06b648b29d2a3e422f73cdb321f6f3c38a2f6a771c4f731344076aaa9","prompt_identity_sha256":"0522abb36692dbdd50684063783240b4ddc0c9bd476d8962448510635525ee0c","raw_response_sha256":"befd190af97048b2bd5fc76ec5dbb0699693aae7b1c77df8e53d7eb379f61466","request_identity_sha256":"adab915de4f3b55074f958c042d6524f8264fd6f05b7831a382505f432e2b94a","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"e5c968c94a6d82629fa48acdb237b3df81e8c4c0674680fd905b9ae5f123f074","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-019","SRC-021","SRC-023"],"review_text":"The proposed doubly recurrent neural network (DRNN) is mathematically well-formulated. The separation of ancestral and fraternal hidden states (Equations 1 and 2) and their combination into a predictive state (Equation 3) provides a clear mechanism for modeling tree topology. The explicit topological prediction via sigmoid projections (Equations 5 and 6) is a sound design choice that avoids the need for artificial padding tokens. The training procedure using back-propagation through structure (BPTS) with a decoupled loss function for labels and topology (Equation 8) is technically consistent and appropriate for the task.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-024","SRC-025","SRC-026","SRC-027","SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The experimental design is adequate for validating the proposed method. The authors use a synthetic dataset to isolate the effect of label content from topological prediction, which is a useful diagnostic. The IFTTT dataset provides a real-world application for mapping sentences to functional programs. The choice of metrics, including F1-score for node and edge retrieval and channel/function accuracy, is appropriate for the noisy nature of the data. The inclusion of a learning curve on the synthetic data (Figure 3) helps demonstrate the model's capacity to scale with data size.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-027","SRC-031"],"review_text":"The paper states that full training details and hyperparameters are provided in the Appendix, but the Appendix is not included in the provided text. The main text mentions the use of cross-validation for hyperparameter selection and the specific data splits for the IFTTT dataset (77,495 train, 5,171 dev, 4,294 test). However, without the Appendix, specific hyperparameters such as learning rates, hidden state dimensions, and regularization techniques are not visible, which hinders full reproducibility. The paper does not explicitly state whether code is available.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-009","SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-029","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The paper provides a thorough comparison against relevant prior work, including the Top-down Tree LSTM (Zhang et al., 2016) and SEQ2TREE (Dong & Lapata, 2016). The related work section clearly distinguishes the proposed method from these approaches, highlighting the explicit topological prediction and end-to-end training. The experimental results in Table 1 show that the DRNN outperforms these baselines on the IFTTT task, supporting the claim of improved performance.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-026","SRC-029","SRC-030"],"review_text":"The paper reports results on the IFTTT dataset but does not provide confidence intervals, standard deviations, or significance tests for the reported improvements. The synthetic experiment mentions averaging over 5 repetitions, but the IFTTT results appear to be from a single run. Without statistical validation, it is difficult to determine if the observed improvements over baselines are statistically significant or due to variance.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"696bd5766f78edc15bf861a95691abda1e75bf8ff74f85ea19383c4146997996","paper_id":"HkYhZDqxg","paper_ordinal":94,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"befd190af97048b2bd5fc76ec5dbb0699693aae7b1c77df8e53d7eb379f61466","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"HkYhZDqxg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"8c72d4118d4ac75b146d3702d1e67f31ab7b4a67218b8b226cba31b97e5890ef","request_identity_sha256":"adab915de4f3b55074f958c042d6524f8264fd6f05b7831a382505f432e2b94a","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":1048,"prompt_tokens":17356,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":18404},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"adab915de4f3b55074f958c042d6524f8264fd6f05b7831a382505f432e2b94a","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}